        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;to the&quot;</strong> is <strong>a single-path philosophical adventure</strong>. where <strong>no two players share the same experience</strong> — a bold, challenging work that <strong>questions modern society</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Game Overview</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is <strong>a philosophical walking simulator</strong> that tests your <strong>memory</strong> and <strong>luck ×</strong> <strong>strategy</strong>. Keep moving forward — your goal is to reach <strong>10,000 meters</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Prove your memory</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Along the way you will be faced with a variety of binary choices. Remember the “correct” choices you encounter; selecting them again later will lengthen the path. Fail to choose correctly and the path shortens.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Crucially, what counts as a “correct” choice differs from player to player</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >— other people’s answers won’t help. What you need is your own memory.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Outstrategize Luck</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You’ll often find yourself facing philosophical dilemmas — “Is love more important than money?” — questions with no single correct answer. At times you can <strong>opt for ‘Luck’</strong> instead of choosing directly. Outcomes are partly governed by chance, but your strategic choices change the odds and the difficulty of those outcomes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4089540/extras/2d3a3faf8fad22658f576fb8a1d7cd08.avif?t=1762605097\" width=960 height=540 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Love or money — which will you choose?</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you fail to extend the path and reach its “terminus” before 10,000 m, it’s game over.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When you finally reach 10,000 m, <strong><u>you will learn a truth that overturns everything</u></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u>— <strong>and realize that the game itself <i>was</i> philosophy.</strong></u></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Story</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You stood on a strange, single road whose length kept changing. With not a scrap of memory, you begin an endless forward march. Exposed to a deluge of knowledge, beasts rush ahead in pursuit of their ideals.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >“End your restless days — question the way you live.”</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Playtime</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >60–240 minutes</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Depends on your effort.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Controls (Keyboard &amp; Mouse)</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >WASD – Move (Press twice to run), Select</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mouse – Look around</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Space – Jump</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Left Click – Examine / Progress dialogue</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Esc – Settings</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Controls (Gamepad)</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Stick – Move / Look around / Select</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A / Button 3 – Jump</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >X / Button 1 – Examine / Progress dialogue</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >START / Button 12 – Settings</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;to the&quot;</strong> is <strong>a single-path philosophical adventure</strong>. where <strong>no two players share the same experience</strong> — a bold, challenging work that <strong>questions modern society</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Game Overview</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is <strong>a philosophical walking simulator</strong> that tests your <strong>memory</strong> and <strong>luck ×</strong> <strong>strategy</strong>. Keep moving forward — your goal is to reach <strong>10,000 meters</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Prove your memory</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Along the way you will be faced with a variety of binary choices. Remember the “correct” choices you encounter; selecting them again later will lengthen the path. Fail to choose correctly and the path shortens.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Crucially, what counts as a “correct” choice differs from player to player</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >— other people’s answers won’t help. What you need is your own memory.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Outstrategize Luck</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You’ll often find yourself facing philosophical dilemmas — “Is love more important than money?” — questions with no single correct answer. At times you can <strong>opt for ‘Luck’</strong> instead of choosing directly. Outcomes are partly governed by chance, but your strategic choices change the odds and the difficulty of those outcomes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4089540/extras/2d3a3faf8fad22658f576fb8a1d7cd08.avif?t=1762605097\" width=960 height=540 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Love or money — which will you choose?</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you fail to extend the path and reach its “terminus” before 10,000 m, it’s game over.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When you finally reach 10,000 m, <strong><u>you will learn a truth that overturns everything</u></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u>— <strong>and realize that the game itself <i>was</i> philosophy.</strong></u></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Story</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You stood on a strange, single road whose length kept changing. With not a scrap of memory, you begin an endless forward march. Exposed to a deluge of knowledge, beasts rush ahead in pursuit of their ideals.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >“End your restless days — question the way you live.”</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Playtime</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >60–240 minutes</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Depends on your effort.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Controls (Keyboard &amp; Mouse)</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >WASD – Move (Press twice to run), Select</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mouse – Look around</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Space – Jump</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Left Click – Examine / Progress dialogue</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Esc – Settings</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Controls (Gamepad)</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Stick – Move / Look around / Select</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A / Button 3 – Jump</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >X / Button 1 – Examine / Progress dialogue</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >START / Button 12 – Settings</p>",
